---
description: Client form schemas vs shared validation
globs: apps/web/src/client/**/schemas/**/*.ts, packages/validation/src/**
---

# Schema

Screen-only form schema: `modules/{context}/schemas/{name}.schema.ts`. Export the schema and its `z.infer` type.

```ts
export const onboardingOrganizationSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().trim().min(1),
});

export type OnboardingOrganizationSchemaType = z.infer<typeof onboardingOrganizationSchema>;
```

An API contract, or a shape validated by both server and client, lives in `@workspace/validation` (`packages/validation/src/modules/{context}/dto/`). The client imports it; never copies it into the module.

```ts
import { completeOnboardingInputDtoSchema } from "@workspace/validation/modules/organization/dto/complete-onboarding.schema";
```

## Shared field schemas

A field shape used in more than one place (email, password, non-empty name, invitation token, etc.) is defined once in `@workspace/validation`, typically `packages/validation/src/shared/{field}.schema.ts`, and imported by DTOs and client form schemas. Never repeat `z.email()` or the like inline across modules.

The canonical schema is **required** (the strictest common case). Relax it at the call site with `.optional()`, `.nullable()`, `.nullish()`, or `.partial()` on the object. Never fork a second validator with different rules.

```ts
// packages/validation/src/shared/email.schema.ts
export const emailSchema = z.email();

// DTO — required
export const verifyCredentialsInputDtoSchema = z.object({
  email: emailSchema,
  password: passwordSchema,
});

// DTO — optional patch
export const updateUserInputDtoSchema = z.object({
  email: emailSchema.optional(),
  name: z.string().trim().min(1).optional(),
});

// Model — nullable column
export const bugReportSchema = z.object({
  reporterEmail: emailSchema.nullable(),
});
```

A new path under `src/shared/` needs a `package.json` `exports` entry.
